A DLL mod that multiplies the runes you gain from every source — killing enemies, using items, selling items, and more. Fully configurable, letting you earn more runes, less runes, or even subtract runes.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
[code]RuneMultiplier=2.0    ; multiplier applied to rune gains from all sources - 1.0 = unchanged, 0 = no runes gained, negative subtracts runes
HotReloadKey=F9       ; key that reloads this file while the game is running
DebugLog=0            ; log extra debug details - 0 disables it[/code]

[b][color=#E74C3C]Only use in offline mode with EAC disabled![/color][/b]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[b]Option 1 - [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url] (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Mod Engine 2 from the link above and extract it into your game folder (the same folder as [i]eldenring.exe[/i]).[/*]
[*]Download this mod, then create a folder to hold it and its INI file - for example, inside your game folder create a [b]natives[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] and edit [b]external_dlls = [ ][/b] to add the DLL, e.g.:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "natives\\RuneMultiplier.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game using Mod Engine 2's launcher, [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Elden Mod Loader from the link above and extract it into your game folder.[/*]
[*]Download this mod and drag [b]RuneMultiplier.dll[/b] and [b]RuneMultiplier.ini[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game - the mod will be loaded automatically.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]2.0[/b]
[list]
[*]Rewritten in Rust - same single AddSoul_Call hook, but the redirect and return jumps are now absolute 64-bit jumps instead of relative ones, so the generated stub no longer needs a nearby-memory search to install.[/*]
[/list]
[b]1.0[/b]
[list]
[*]Multiplies rune gains from every source via a single hook on AddSoul_Call.[/*]
[/list]